    "title": "KIPP Capital Region opens newly constructed high school - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Courtney Ward ,\n37 minutes ago\nALBANY, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — KIPP Capital Region Public Schools celebrated the opening of its newly constructed high school in Albany on Wednesday. It will be the first co-ed charter high school in the city.\nDownload our WTEN+ streaming app on Roku, Fire TV and Apple TV! Starting in the fall, the school welcomes 400 students for the 2025-2026 school year. Officials said they have plans to grow to 800 students when they reach full capacity across grades 9 through 12.\nThe school is located off Northern Boulevard in Albany. It will officially open for classes on Tuesday, Sept. 2.\nRead the latest from NEWS10:\nNEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader!\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
